        {
            "content_html": "<img src=\"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/349114?u=1185d4fc45f5ff4c4a592b30a4dd2bb5cd1b7128&v=4\" width=\"64\" height=\"64\" alt=\"\"/><br/><h3 dir=\"auto\">Description</h3>\n<p dir=\"auto\">This PR adds a new page to our list of \"attacks\", this one is on JavaScript Prototype Pollution.</p>\n<p dir=\"auto\">It's a draft for now. Still trying to learn more about this myself. I want to add another example scenario \"Pollution via JSON.parse and object merging/cloning\" but I don't fully understand it yet and haven't been able to get myself polluted this way :) Maybe this has been fixed in JS engines? Any pointers appreciated.</p>\n<p dir=\"auto\">Generally, I'm not sure if I covered everything that needs to appear here. I think I'm somewhat happy about the defenses part, but explaining how to actually get into to polluting objects might need some more words?</p>\n<p dir=\"auto\">Also, I think this needs integration into JS docs (at a minimum some linkage).</p>\n<h3 dir=\"auto\">Motivation</h3>\n<p dir=\"auto\">Developing a series of guides about common attacks on websites, explaining for each attack: how it works, the impact, and how to defend against it.</p>\n<h3 dir=\"auto\">Additional details</h3>\n<p dir=\"auto\">Would love some feedback from <a class=\"user-mention notranslate\" data-hovercard-type=\"user\" data-hovercard-url=\"/users/wbamberg/hovercard\" data-octo-click=\"hovercard-link-click\" data-octo-dimensions=\"link_type:self\" href=\"https://github.com/wbamberg\">@wbamberg</a>, <a class=\"user-mention notranslate\" data-hovercard-type=\"user\" data-hovercard-url=\"/users/aaronshim/hovercard\" data-octo-click=\"hovercard-link-click\" data-octo-dimensions=\"link_type:self\" href=\"https://github.com/aaronshim\">@aaronshim</a> and maybe <a class=\"user-mention notranslate\" data-hovercard-type=\"user\" data-hovercard-url=\"/users/Josh-Cena/hovercard\" data-octo-click=\"hovercard-link-click\" data-octo-dimensions=\"link_type:self\" href=\"https://github.com/Josh-Cena\">@Josh-Cena</a>.</p>\n<h3 dir=\"auto\">Related issues and pull requests</h3>\n<p dir=\"auto\">None, I think.</p>",
            "url": "https://github.com/mdn/content/pull/41260",
            "title": "Add a page for JavaScript prototype pollution attack",
            "date_modified": "2025-09-23T18:26:48.000Z",
            "date_published": "2025-09-23T17:43:52.000Z",
            "author": {
                "name": "Elchi3",
                "url": "https://github.com/Elchi3"
            }
        },
        {
            "content_html": "<img src=\"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/47647?u=2fbfc431a85d357f00c0146d5e55b425b7f00a3d&v=4\" width=\"64\" height=\"64\" alt=\"\"/><br/>\n\n<h3 dir=\"auto\">Description</h3>\n<p dir=\"auto\">Chrome 136 introduces the CSS <a href=\"https://drafts.csswg.org/css-color-hdr/#the-dynamic-range-limit-property\" rel=\"nofollow\"><code class=\"notranslate\">dynamic-range-limit</code></a> property; see <a href=\"https://chromestatus.com/feature/5146250411769856\" rel=\"nofollow\">https://chromestatus.com/feature/5146250411769856</a>.</p>\n<p dir=\"auto\">The <code class=\"notranslate\">dynamic-range-limit-mix()</code> function is also supported, but I'm not sure which version of Chrome this first appeared in. I've asked Chrome engineering for an answer to this question.</p>\n<p dir=\"auto\">This PR documents both of the two features mentioned above.</p>\n<div class=\"markdown-alert markdown-alert-note\" dir=\"auto\"><p class=\"markdown-alert-title\" dir=\"auto\"><svg class=\"octicon octicon-info mr-2\" viewBox=\"0 0 16 16\" version=\"1.1\" width=\"16\" height=\"16\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><path d=\"M0 8a8 8 0 1 1 16 0A8 8 0 0 1 0 8Zm8-6.5a6.5 6.5 0 1 0 0 13 6.5 6.5 0 0 0 0-13ZM6.5 7.75A.75.75 0 0 1 7.25 7h1a.75.75 0 0 1 .75.75v2.75h.25a.75.75 0 0 1 0 1.5h-2a.75.75 0 0 1 0-1.5h.25v-2h-.25a.75.75 0 0 1-.75-.75ZM8 6a1 1 0 1 1 0-2 1 1 0 0 1 0 2Z\"></path></svg>Note</p><p dir=\"auto\">Some of the description in the property page might want to go into a separate glossary entry, but I wasn't sure how best to chop up this information. Opinions welcome.</p>\n</div>\n\n<h3 dir=\"auto\">Motivation</h3>\n\n<h3 dir=\"auto\">Additional details</h3>\n\n<h3 dir=\"auto\">Related issues and pull requests</h3>\n\n\n\n",
            "url": "https://github.com/mdn/content/pull/41257",
            "title": "Editorial review: Document CSS dynamic-range-limit",
